雪落寒山 Snowfall Peak — Isle Film (方寸影像), a NEO-Cine library demo

THE WORLD: 雪落寒山 (Snowfall Peak), the second isle of NEO-Isle (方寸之境), https://github.com/neohoy/neo-isle,
  MIT, (c) 2026 NEO造物集 (neohoy), the library author. world.js is copied from NEO-Isle's examples/02-雪落寒山/world.js
  unchanged (a note at its top says so). Everything in the picture is that isle as NEO-Isle builds it: the film only chooses
  the camera, the hour and the isle's clock.

ENGINE: NEO-Isle's engine (fangcun.js and template.html), version 1.2.0 with its film mode, pinned in ../kit/isle-core/
  (MIT, its LICENSE and SOURCE are there), synced by ../kit/tools/sync_isle.sh. three.js r170 (MIT, (c) 2010-2024 three.js
  authors), the library's own node_modules/three.

FONTS (SIL Open Font License 1.1; fetched by ../kit/tools/fonts.py from github.com/google/fonts at commit 86aced91 into
  out/fonts-src/, subset to the characters the film prints into fonts/*.ttf; none kept in git; licence texts in fonts/):
- Noto Serif SC, Copyright 2012 Google Inc.: Chinese title, subtitles, end card
  (fonts/NSerif-300.ttf, fonts/NSerif-400.ttf, instances of the variable font).
- Cormorant Garamond, Copyright 2015 the Cormorant Project Authors (github.com/CatharsisFonts/Cormorant): English lines and the sign-off (fonts/CG-500.ttf, fonts/CGI-500.ttf).

SOUND: synthesized in code (numpy and the library's core/audio/sfx.py filters), no recordings, samples or existing music:
  ../kit/tools/mix.py (wind, snow, crows, the hour chimes, the glass, the wonder, the score in D at 80 BPM). No narration.

TOOLS: the NEO-Cine library's core/ tools, which are Lemo-Opuscar's (MIT, (c) 2026 LemoLab): headless Chrome frame capture,
  events export, reading-time check, ffmpeg encode and loudness master; neo/audio/cues.py, neo/audio/master.py.

ON SCREEN: the title card names the work (方寸之境 · 第二境, 雪落寒山, Snowfall Peak); the end card signs off with NEO-Cine and
  the style's name only.
